Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-12T07:10:22.6470334Z   PR_BODY: ### Summary
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	Fixes #37416.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	### Problem & Background
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	Django previously recorded applied migrations inside the schema editor context to keep schema changes and their corresponding entries in `django_migrations` within the same transaction.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	However, #32374 moved migration recording outside the schema editor context when deferred SQL was present. This was necessary to ensure that a migration would not be recorded as applied if executing its deferred SQL failed.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	The change introduced an atomicity issue. Deferred SQL is executed when the schema editor context exits, so the database transaction may commit before Django records the migration. If the process crashes or recording fails during this interval, the schema changes remain in the database even though Django has no record that the migration was applied.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	This can cause Django to attempt the migration again, potentially failing because the schema objects already exist. Recording migrations outside the transaction also adds unnecessary overhead when a squashed migration records many replaced migrations individually.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	### Solution
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Added `execute_deferred_sql()` to `BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor` to execute pending deferred SQL statements and clear the list.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Updated `BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor.__exit__()` to use the new method, preserving the existing deferred SQL execution behavior.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Updated `MigrationExecutor.apply_migration()` to execute deferred SQL and record the migration before exiting the schema editor context.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Applied the same approach to `MigrationExecutor.unapply_migration()` to keep migration reversal and its recording consistent.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Ensured that deferred SQL is executed before migration recording, so a deferred SQL failure prevents the migration from being recorded prematurely.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Added regression tests for atomic migration recording during application and reversal, along with a unit test for deferred SQL execution.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	### Testing
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Added `test_migrations_applied_and_recorded_atomically_deferred_sql` in `tests/migrations/test_executor.py`.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Added `test_migrations_unapplied_and_recorded_atomically` in `tests/migrations/test_executor.py`.
Run Quality Checks on a PR	UNKNOWN STEP	- Added `test_execute_deferred_sql` in `tests/schema/tests.py`.
